{"name":"Infatuation","hex":"#f0d5ea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"infatuation","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An immensely strong love or sexual attraction.","The act of infatuating; the state of being infatuated; madness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infatuation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Infatuation","blocks":[{"text":"Infatuation refers to being \"in love\" or intensely \"love smitten\", with possible connotations of youth, irrationality, foolishness, or capriciousness. An individual may be considered infatuated with a person they do not know well yet, or whom others view as unsuitable. In the triangular theory of love, \"infatuation\" refers to romantic passion in the absence of intimacy or commitment, as in love at first sight and limerence. A simple infatuation which is more short-lived may be referred to as a crush, or \"puppy love\" in adolescence. Infatuation might also be compared to the \"honeymoon phase\" of a relationship."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e9/Uluchi_Arujann.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infatuation","wikidata":"Q1320124"},{"title":"Infatuation (Rod Stewart song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Infatuation\" is a 1984 song by Rod Stewart from his thirteenth studio album Camouflage, written by Stewart, Duane Hitchings and Roland Robinson released as the first single from the album."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infatuation_(Rod_Stewart_song)","wikidata":"Q6029147"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg/500px-Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg/1280px-Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg/500px-Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Counterfeit money versus real money","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Photo_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg/500px-Photo_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Photo_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg/500px-Photo_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Albert Ellis c. 1966","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhoto_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg"}],"sounds":{"infatuation":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/98/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-infatuation.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/98/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-infatuation.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-infatuation.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/98/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-infatuation.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-infatuation.wav.ogg"}]}}}